  ],
  "patch_scope": "Bazel-compatible core set methods/constructor, assignment-specific mutation, scoped iterator error cleanup and regressions; allocation-free typed BigInt inspection for native JSON preflight; Bazel 9.3 UTF-8 byte-string string methods (ASCII-only case mapping/predicates, ASCII strip whitespace, explicit None strip argument, byte-wise title letter state) and Printer-compatible string repr escaping; location-aware indexing and `in` (StarlarkValue::at_with_location / is_in_with_location with default delegation to at / is_in, used by the ArrayIndex and In bytecode instructions with the expression's lazily computed span) for native ctx.toolchains string keys (docs/TOOLCHAINS.md); Bazel 9.3 StructImpl struct repr (sorted `name = value` fields), BuiltinFunction repr of native functions and bound methods (with an optional builtin receiver for module values such as `native`/`attr`), str()-based `%s`/single-`{}` formatting without `!r`/`!s` conversions (`Missing argument`), `builtin_function_or_method` type (unhashable, as in Bazel) of native functions and bound methods, `<function NAME from FILE>` def/lambda repr, and a `StarlarkValue::collect_debug_print` hook (default `str()`) used by `print`/`fail` (Bazel debugPrint); Bazel's `unhashable type: 'T'` error text; the crate's own tests, doc test, starlark-go testcase and 29 goldens (regenerated with STARLARK_RUST_REGENERATE_GOLDEN_TESTS=1) updated to these behaviours, see BAZEL_RS_MODIFICATIONS.md. Native feature installation remains separate from vendor changes. Bazel 9.3 frozen list/dict mutation text ('trying to mutate a frozen list|dict value', Starlark.checkMutable) and a reverse `|` hook (StarlarkValue::rbit_or) so a dict left operand defers to `select()` (SelectorList.binaryOp with thisLeft = false), also for `|=`. The vendored crate's own frozen list/dict mutation tests and error-display goldens expect that Bazel text (tuples, bytes and sets keep `Immutable`). A value-specific unknown-attribute message hook (StarlarkValue::unknown_attribute_message, default None) used by attribute reads and Value::get_attr_error, for Bazel's ctx.outputs/ctx.executable getErrorMessageForUnknownField texts. N26: Bazel 9.3 string literal values (raw strings keep backslashes; BUILD/.bzl analysis byte escapes decode as UTF-8 with replacement; eval.rs), per-thread Latin-1 char model selection for repository/extension evaluation (values/types/string.rs), split/rsplit with a required string sep, elems() as a list, and Latin-1 isspace/title/capitalize (methods.rs). N18c: getattr(x, name) without a default also consults StarlarkValue::unknown_attribute_message (Bazel Starlark.getattr with Structure.getErrorMessageForUnknownField), used by the Starlark transition attr struct. N33: Bazel 9.3 interpreter error texts: def/builtin argument binding (StarlarkFunction/BuiltinFunction ArgumentProcessor order and texts, replayed on the cold error path of ParametersSpec, also for positional-only builtins bound by generated code and the set constructor), call-argument */** texts, 'unsupported binary operation'/'unsupported comparison'/unary/not-callable/not-iterable/slice/len/field-assignment texts, `'T' value has no field or method 'x'` with Bazel's SpellChecker hint (struct lists its fields), `name 'x' is not defined`, `dictionary expression has duplicate key: REPR`, `'in <string>'` and list/tuple/set iterable parameter texts; the crate's own tests, two doc tests and three goldens follow them. N33 follow-up: struct values are unordered like Bazel's StructImpl; `*args` elements bind after named arguments and may overwrite them (StarlarkFunction/BuiltinFunction addPositionalArg); builtin argument types are checked while binding, before the positional count (native parameter types kept on NativeFunc/NativeMeth); Bazel's @Param names and kinds for string/list/dict methods and MethodLibrary builtins (find/rfind/index/rindex/count/startswith/endswith `sub`, partition `sep`, join `elements`, range `start_or_stop`/`stop`, list `item`/`items`/`x`/`i`, named dict.get/setdefault `default`, positional sorted `key`, named enumerate `list`, required int `x`, fail `msg`/`attr`/`sep`/`stack_trace`, print `sep`) and join's element text. N48: Bazel 9.3's rejection of recursive calls (StarlarkThread.isRecursiveCall, StarlarkFunction.java:571-574): after argument binding, calling a def or lambda whose code (its DefInfo, not the closure) is already executing in the evaluator fails with `function 'NAME' called recursively`, located at the def identifier or lambda start (new DefInfo.identifier_span, Bazel's innermost traceback frame); the evaluator keeps a boxed stack of executing DefInfo pointers (builtins such as a sorted(key = ...) callback's are not tracked, nor are inlinable bodies, which cannot call Starlark code); Evaluator::set_allow_recursion (Bazel's -allow_recursion, default false) and Evaluator::with_new_recursion_scope (for callbacks Bazel runs in a new StarlarkThread: symbolic macro implementations, computed defaults, map_each); only function bodies whose calls cannot run Starlark code (builtins that never call an argument, string constant methods, no function-valued constant arguments) are still inlined, since an inlined function has no frame; the crate's own tests follow (funcall_test expects the Bazel text and keeps its call-stack-overflow checks with recursion allowed, the Go function.star `option:recursion` chunk runs with recursion allowed, two def_inline goldens regenerated) and src/tests/call.rs and src/tests/opt/def_inline.rs add tests. Portable def and lambda values for bazel-rs's analysis snapshot (docs/STARLARK_VENDOR.md \"Portable def and lambda values\"): modules keep the DefInfo of every compiled function, PortableDef takes a frozen function apart (code location, parameter defaults, captured values) and instantiates it again against a module evaluated from the same source, and ParametersSpec rebuilds a def parameter list.",
